[{"text": "The assembly will now hear an address by", "start": 4.4, "duration": 4.919}, {"text": "his excellency", "start": 6.16, "duration": 3.159}, {"text": "enjimi,", "start": 11.28, "duration": 3.0}, {"text": "vice president of the United Republic of", "start": 15.839, "duration": 4.721}, {"text": "Tanzania.", "start": 18.48, "duration": 4.799}, {"text": "I request protocol to escort his", "start": 20.56, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "excellency and invite him to address the", "start": 23.279, "duration": 5.801}, {"text": "assembly.", "start": 26.08, "duration": 3.0}, {"text": "Your Excellency", "start": 40.0, "duration": 5.84}, {"text": "Dr. Halier Rahman, President of the 81st", "start": 41.92, "duration": 6.56}, {"text": "session of the United Nations General", "start": 45.84, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "Assembly. Your Excellency Antonio", "start": 48.48, "duration": 6.48}, {"text": "Gutirez, Secretary General of the United", "start": 51.6, "duration": 6.639}, {"text": "Nations. Excellencies, heads of state", "start": 54.96, "duration": 6.079}, {"text": "and government, distinguished delegates,", "start": 58.239, "duration": 4.881}, {"text": "good afternoon.", "start": 61.039, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "It is indeed a great honor and privilege", "start": 63.12, "duration": 5.679}, {"text": "to address this assembly on behalf of", "start": 66.159, "duration": 5.921}, {"text": "her excellency Dr. Samir Sulu Hassan,", "start": 68.799, "duration": 5.281}, {"text": "President of the United Republic of", "start": 72.08, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "Tanzania. Her excellency, the president,", "start": 74.08, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "asked me to convey her fraternal", "start": 77.68, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "greetings and best wishes for the", "start": 79.6, "duration": 7.04}, {"text": "success of this session. Mr. President,", "start": 82.32, "duration": 6.4}, {"text": "allow me to congratulate you on your", "start": 86.64, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "election to preside over the 81st", "start": 88.72, "duration": 5.039}, {"text": "session of the United Nations General", "start": 91.6, "duration": 3.92}, {"text": "Assembly.", "start": 93.759, "duration": 4.161}, {"text": "Your immense experience and diplomatic", "start": 95.52, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "skills give us confidence in your", "start": 97.92, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "ability to guide the proceedings of this", "start": 100.64, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "session successfully.", "start": 103.52, "duration": 6.08}, {"text": "Your election is also a fitting tribute", "start": 106.24, "duration": 6.72}, {"text": "to the great country Bangladesh", "start": 109.6, "duration": 6.159}, {"text": "with which Tanzania enjoys excellent", "start": 112.96, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "relations.", "start": 115.759, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "Mr. president.", "start": 118.0, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "About 80 years ago,", "start": 120.399, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "the United Nation was founded in San", "start": 122.88, "duration": 5.599}, {"text": "Francisco on a simple but enduring", "start": 125.119, "duration": 7.361}, {"text": "principle that nations can prevent war", "start": 128.479, "duration": 7.041}, {"text": "and advance peace through trust,", "start": 132.48, "duration": 6.399}, {"text": "collective action, and respect the UN", "start": 135.52, "duration": 6.4}, {"text": "charter. Today,", "start": 138.879, "duration": 5.681}, {"text": "war and insecurity are not only", "start": 141.92, "duration": 5.84}, {"text": "existential threats to our survival, but", "start": 144.56, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "a range of challenges, including climate", "start": 147.76, "duration": 6.479}, {"text": "change, pandemics, ungoverned artificial", "start": 150.56, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "intelligence,", "start": 154.239, "duration": 4.321}, {"text": "and energy insecurity, just to mention a", "start": 155.84, "duration": 5.92}, {"text": "few. These challenges", "start": 158.56, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "should remind us of a need for a", "start": 161.76, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "stronger and much more coordinated", "start": 164.16, "duration": 7.04}, {"text": "United Nations. Therefore, the theme of", "start": 167.36, "duration": 7.519}, {"text": "this session that is restoring trust,", "start": 171.2, "duration": 6.399}, {"text": "managing transformation, a united nation", "start": 174.879, "duration": 6.72}, {"text": "that delivers for all is timely for it", "start": 177.599, "duration": 6.56}, {"text": "requires us to revert to the founding", "start": 181.599, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "principles of maintaining peace and", "start": 184.159, "duration": 6.561}, {"text": "restoring trust.", "start": 187.599, "duration": 5.441}, {"text": "Managing transformation requires", "start": 190.72, "duration": 5.439}, {"text": "reforming the UN to meet the realities", "start": 193.04, "duration": 5.199}, {"text": "of our time.", "start": 196.159, "duration": 4.881}, {"text": "In that regard, I commend our", "start": 198.239, "duration": 4.881}, {"text": "illustrious secretary general, his", "start": 201.04, "duration": 4.559}, {"text": "excellency Antonio Gutirez for", "start": 203.12, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "championing the UN80 initiative that", "start": 205.599, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "aims to advance the transformation", "start": 208.72, "duration": 3.92}, {"text": "agenda.", "start": 210.879, "duration": 5.92}, {"text": "In our opinion, the UN80 initiative must", "start": 212.64, "duration": 7.2}, {"text": "go beyond administrative efficiency to", "start": 216.799, "duration": 5.041}, {"text": "include overall organizational", "start": 219.84, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "effectiveness, accountability, and", "start": 221.84, "duration": 5.039}, {"text": "representativeness for the United Nation", "start": 224.08, "duration": 6.239}, {"text": "to be able to deliver for all.", "start": 226.879, "duration": 6.481}, {"text": "Further, the transformation must be", "start": 230.319, "duration": 6.401}, {"text": "undertaken with utmost caution to avoid", "start": 233.36, "duration": 5.519}, {"text": "going off track on the development", "start": 236.72, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "pillar and incapacitating the United", "start": 238.879, "duration": 6.881}, {"text": "Nation country offices and programs.", "start": 241.84, "duration": 6.8}, {"text": "Mr. President, excellencies and", "start": 245.76, "duration": 6.399}, {"text": "distinguished delegates.", "start": 248.64, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "While we're a few years away from year", "start": 252.159, "duration": 4.241}, {"text": "2030,", "start": 254.64, "duration": 4.879}, {"text": "progress towards attainment of the SDGs", "start": 256.4, "duration": 6.16}, {"text": "is still unimpressive.", "start": 259.519, "duration": 6.081}, {"text": "Given this situation, we need to improve", "start": 262.56, "duration": 7.199}, {"text": "our execution and ensure that every cent", "start": 265.6, "duration": 8.08}, {"text": "invested delivers results.", "start": 269.759, "duration": 7.601}, {"text": "Tanzania remains committed and has made", "start": 273.68, "duration": 7.28}, {"text": "strides in implementing the 2030 agenda.", "start": 277.36, "duration": 7.52}, {"text": "Tanzania's development vision 2050 aims", "start": 280.96, "duration": 6.799}, {"text": "to build an inclusive and competitive", "start": 284.88, "duration": 6.319}, {"text": "economy that ensures quality of life for", "start": 287.759, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "all.", "start": 291.199, "duration": 3.681}, {"text": "We're investing in our people,", "start": 292.639, "duration": 4.881}, {"text": "productive infrastructure, technology,", "start": 294.88, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "and innovation while creating greater", "start": 297.52, "duration": 5.92}, {"text": "opportunity for women and young people.", "start": 300.24, "duration": 6.08}, {"text": "Our ambition is to transform economic", "start": 303.44, "duration": 6.16}, {"text": "growth into lasting improvements for", "start": 306.32, "duration": 6.08}, {"text": "people's lives.", "start": 309.6, "duration": 6.08}, {"text": "These ambitions may not be realized if", "start": 312.4, "duration": 5.519}, {"text": "the international financial architecture", "start": 315.68, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "is not made to work for development.", "start": 317.919, "duration": 6.961}, {"text": "Currently, when developing countries are", "start": 321.68, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "accelerating progress,", "start": 324.88, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "they are restricted by higher borrowing", "start": 327.28, "duration": 6.4}, {"text": "costs, rising debt burdens, and limited", "start": 329.84, "duration": 6.88}, {"text": "access to affordable long-term", "start": 333.68, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "financing.", "start": 336.72, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "Tanzania stresses that improvements must", "start": 338.4, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "be made to ensure expansion of", "start": 341.28, "duration": 6.08}, {"text": "concessional financing, mobilization of", "start": 344.4, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "private investment, improved access to", "start": 347.36, "duration": 5.679}, {"text": "development and climate finance and", "start": 350.16, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "giving developing countries a stronger", "start": 353.039, "duration": 5.281}, {"text": "voice in the global financial decision", "start": 355.36, "duration": 5.839}, {"text": "making.", "start": 358.32, "duration": 6.08}, {"text": "It is without a doubt that political", "start": 361.199, "duration": 6.241}, {"text": "commitment is paramount in undertaking", "start": 364.4, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "focused investment.", "start": 367.44, "duration": 5.039}, {"text": "In that, Tanzania has made significant", "start": 369.6, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "strides in reducing maternal and child", "start": 372.479, "duration": 5.84}, {"text": "mortality by expanding facility delivery", "start": 374.96, "duration": 10.079}, {"text": "from 51% in 2015 to 81% in 2022.", "start": 378.319, "duration": 9.921}, {"text": "Our experience on this demonstrates that", "start": 385.039, "duration": 5.921}, {"text": "when invest when we invest in feasible", "start": 388.24, "duration": 5.519}, {"text": "projects and remain people centered", "start": 390.96, "duration": 6.239}, {"text": "development can move from promises to", "start": 393.759, "duration": 6.801}, {"text": "measurable results.", "start": 397.199, "duration": 6.401}, {"text": "It is in this spirit that her excellency", "start": 400.56, "duration": 5.919}, {"text": "president Samya Sulu Hassan accepted the", "start": 403.6, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "responsibility of championing maternal", "start": 406.479, "duration": 6.081}, {"text": "and child health for the African Union.", "start": 409.12, "duration": 6.079}, {"text": "Under her leadership, Tanzania reduced", "start": 412.56, "duration": 7.359}, {"text": "maternal deaths by 80% in just seven", "start": 415.199, "duration": 7.72}, {"text": "years.", "start": 419.919, "duration": 3.0}, {"text": "We now aim to advance the three zeros.", "start": 423.199, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "Zero preventable maternal and child", "start": 427.36, "duration": 6.239}, {"text": "deaths, zero home deliveries, and zero", "start": 429.199, "duration": 6.961}, {"text": "unvaccinated children.", "start": 433.599, "duration": 5.121}, {"text": "Our experience shows that this is an", "start": 436.16, "duration": 5.039}, {"text": "agenda that Africa can successfully", "start": 438.72, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "achieve, but it will require sustained", "start": 441.199, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "political leadership, adequate", "start": 444.24, "duration": 5.519}, {"text": "financing, and stronger partnerships. We", "start": 446.479, "duration": 5.361}, {"text": "therefore urge the international", "start": 449.759, "duration": 4.961}, {"text": "community to join us in giving this", "start": 451.84, "duration": 7.28}, {"text": "agenda a big push.", "start": 454.72, "duration": 7.199}, {"text": "Excellencies,", "start": 459.12, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "our efforts to address climate related", "start": 461.919, "duration": 4.961}, {"text": "challenges continue to face", "start": 464.56, "duration": 3.84}, {"text": "unjustifiable", "start": 466.88, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "obstacles mainly from those contributing", "start": 468.4, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "significantly to greenhouse gas", "start": 471.84, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "emissions.", "start": 474.4, "duration": 4.16}, {"text": "Global efforts to address climate", "start": 476.16, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "challenges are being frustrated by", "start": 478.56, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "withdrawal of financial contributions", "start": 481.36, "duration": 4.959}, {"text": "supporting climate adaptation measures", "start": 484.0, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "and initiatives by international and", "start": 486.319, "duration": 4.801}, {"text": "regional institutions as well as", "start": 488.72, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "individual states.", "start": 491.12, "duration": 5.359}, {"text": "Let us prioritize delivery on the", "start": 493.52, "duration": 5.92}, {"text": "pledges for climate action by increasing", "start": 496.479, "duration": 5.521}, {"text": "long-term concessional financing and", "start": 499.44, "duration": 6.479}, {"text": "development of newer technologies.", "start": 502.0, "duration": 6.8}, {"text": "On this agenda, Tanzania chose to", "start": 505.919, "duration": 4.801}, {"text": "address the just energy transition", "start": 508.8, "duration": 5.679}, {"text": "component through different measures.", "start": 510.72, "duration": 6.64}, {"text": "Some of these measures include", "start": 514.479, "duration": 5.521}, {"text": "implementation of the national renewable", "start": 517.36, "duration": 6.799}, {"text": "strategy that comprises of a 2,115", "start": 520.0, "duration": 7.76}, {"text": "megawatt Julius Ner hydro power project", "start": 524.159, "duration": 8.321}, {"text": "of 650 megawatts of solar and wind power", "start": 527.76, "duration": 6.32}, {"text": "projects,", "start": 532.48, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "130 megawatts of geothermal uh power", "start": 534.08, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "projects, and the national clean cooking", "start": 537.44, "duration": 6.399}, {"text": "strategy which aims to ensure that 80%", "start": 540.08, "duration": 7.439}, {"text": "of households adopt clean cooking by the", "start": 543.839, "duration": 6.881}, {"text": "year 2034.", "start": 547.519, "duration": 5.201}, {"text": "In our efforts to reduce the use of", "start": 550.72, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "fossil fuels, we have also opted for the", "start": 552.72, "duration": 5.679}, {"text": "electric railway to link the port of", "start": 556.0, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "Daris Salam to neighboring countries of", "start": 558.399, "duration": 5.601}, {"text": "Burundi and the Democratic Republic of", "start": 561.04, "duration": 6.56}, {"text": "Congo. We therefore appeal that climate", "start": 564.0, "duration": 6.72}, {"text": "financing be provided as grants and", "start": 567.6, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "concessional financing to step up", "start": 570.72, "duration": 5.679}, {"text": "efforts on climate action.", "start": 572.88, "duration": 5.92}, {"text": "Mr. President,", "start": 576.399, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "Tanzania joins small island and coastal", "start": 578.8, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "states in pushing for a workable", "start": 581.519, "duration": 6.801}, {"text": "solution to address sea level rises.", "start": 584.0, "duration": 7.68}, {"text": "We commend the president for conveying", "start": 588.32, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "today the high level event addressing", "start": 591.68, "duration": 5.279}, {"text": "the existential threats posed by sea", "start": 594.32, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "level rise and we look forward to the", "start": 596.959, "duration": 5.681}, {"text": "adoption of the UN declaration on sea", "start": 599.92, "duration": 5.039}, {"text": "level rise which will provide a", "start": 602.64, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "comprehensive framework for", "start": 604.959, "duration": 4.401}, {"text": "international cooperation scientific", "start": 607.04, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "advancement adaptation resilience and", "start": 609.36, "duration": 5.919}, {"text": "legal stability.", "start": 612.48, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "We welcome the declaration's legal", "start": 615.279, "duration": 6.401}, {"text": "affirmation on the stability of maritime", "start": 618.0, "duration": 6.959}, {"text": "zones under United Nation Convention on", "start": 621.68, "duration": 6.32}, {"text": "Law of the Seas and the continuity of", "start": 624.959, "duration": 6.081}, {"text": "statehood even in cases of physical land", "start": 628.0, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "loss while encouraging strengthened", "start": 631.04, "duration": 4.799}, {"text": "international cooperation and the", "start": 633.44, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "protection of human rights.", "start": 635.839, "duration": 4.881}, {"text": "Timely and urgent action is needed to", "start": 638.48, "duration": 4.16}, {"text": "safeguard the future of our coastal", "start": 640.72, "duration": 5.92}, {"text": "communities and island nations.", "start": 642.64, "duration": 7.0}, {"text": "Excellencies,", "start": 646.64, "duration": 3.0}, {"text": "global solidarity", "start": 649.68, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "must be concurrent with respect of each", "start": 651.839, "duration": 5.601}, {"text": "other's sovereignity.", "start": 655.2, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "Tanzania stands against the", "start": 657.44, "duration": 4.959}, {"text": "proliferating trend of some states to", "start": 659.44, "duration": 6.079}, {"text": "assume the responsibility of policing", "start": 662.399, "duration": 6.401}, {"text": "and imposing unilateral sanctions on", "start": 665.519, "duration": 5.681}, {"text": "others, thus undermining the principles", "start": 668.8, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "of sovereignity and peaceful", "start": 671.2, "duration": 4.079}, {"text": "coexistence.", "start": 673.76, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "As stated previously, Tanzania reaffirms", "start": 675.279, "duration": 5.601}, {"text": "its position to oppose the use of such", "start": 678.24, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "coercive measures against any member", "start": 680.88, "duration": 4.959}, {"text": "state and reaffirms its unwavering", "start": 683.36, "duration": 6.64}, {"text": "solidarity with Cuba, Zimbabwe, and all", "start": 685.839, "duration": 7.361}, {"text": "other states that are subjected to such", "start": 690.0, "duration": 7.36}, {"text": "unjustifiable constraints.", "start": 693.2, "duration": 6.56}, {"text": "In line with this,", "start": 697.36, "duration": 6.08}, {"text": "our resolve to leave no one behind.", "start": 699.76, "duration": 6.56}, {"text": "We call for an immediate and unequivocal", "start": 703.44, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "lifting of these measures that cause", "start": 706.32, "duration": 5.92}, {"text": "hardship, constrain development, and", "start": 709.2, "duration": 8.0}, {"text": "obstruct full enjoyment of human rights.", "start": 712.24, "duration": 7.52}, {"text": "Mr. President,", "start": 717.2, "duration": 5.92}, {"text": "global peace and security are vital for", "start": 719.76, "duration": 6.319}, {"text": "sustainable soioeconomic development.", "start": 723.12, "duration": 5.92}, {"text": "The United Nations through its charter", "start": 726.079, "duration": 5.521}, {"text": "has remained central to international", "start": 729.04, "duration": 6.4}, {"text": "efforts to maintain peace and security,", "start": 731.6, "duration": 6.32}, {"text": "uphold international law, promote", "start": 735.44, "duration": 6.399}, {"text": "conditions conducive to development.", "start": 737.92, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "However,", "start": 741.839, "duration": 4.641}, {"text": "despite these longlasting commitments,", "start": 743.44, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "the persistence of armed conflicts", "start": 746.48, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "around the world reflect the departure", "start": 749.04, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "from the purpose and principles of the", "start": 751.92, "duration": 4.719}, {"text": "charter.", "start": 754.56, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "In addition, there are emerging", "start": 756.639, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "challenges to the authority of the", "start": 758.88, "duration": 4.079}, {"text": "United Nations Charter and the", "start": 760.959, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "established principles of international", "start": 762.959, "duration": 5.201}, {"text": "law, often without commensurate", "start": 764.959, "duration": 4.961}, {"text": "accountability.", "start": 768.16, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "These developments underscore the urgent", "start": 769.92, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "need to reaffirm multilateralism,", "start": 772.88, "duration": 6.24}, {"text": "strengthen respect for international law", "start": 775.92, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "and reinforce the central role of the", "start": 779.12, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "United Nations in maintaining", "start": 781.68, "duration": 6.719}, {"text": "international peace and security.", "start": 784.32, "duration": 7.28}, {"text": "In that regard, Tanzania remains firmly", "start": 788.399, "duration": 6.24}, {"text": "committed to supporting the efforts of", "start": 791.6, "duration": 6.239}, {"text": "the UN Security Council to fulfill its", "start": 794.639, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "primary responsibility for the", "start": 797.839, "duration": 5.201}, {"text": "maintainance of international peace and", "start": 800.079, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "security.", "start": 803.04, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "Our commitment is demonstrated by our", "start": 804.959, "duration": 6.081}, {"text": "two terms of service on the Security", "start": 807.76, "duration": 6.72}, {"text": "Council during which we made substantive", "start": 811.04, "duration": 7.599}, {"text": "contributions to such cause.", "start": 814.48, "duration": 6.64}, {"text": "Notable achievements include the", "start": 818.639, "duration": 4.801}, {"text": "adoption of security council resol", "start": 821.12, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "resolution 1653", "start": 823.44, "duration": 6.399}, {"text": "in the year 20 uh 20006 on the great", "start": 825.76, "duration": 6.079}, {"text": "lakes region and Tanzania's", "start": 829.839, "duration": 3.841}, {"text": "collaboration with Denmark in", "start": 831.839, "duration": 4.081}, {"text": "establishing the peacebuilding", "start": 833.68, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "commission.", "start": 835.92, "duration": 3.68}, {"text": "Excellencies,", "start": 837.68, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "building on this record", "start": 839.6, "duration": 5.039}, {"text": "and sustained commitment to", "start": 842.56, "duration": 3.68}, {"text": "multilateralism,", "start": 844.639, "duration": 5.921}, {"text": "I am pleased to inform you that", "start": 846.24, "duration": 8.24}, {"text": "recently the African Union formally took", "start": 850.56, "duration": 5.519}, {"text": "note", "start": 854.48, "duration": 4.08}, {"text": "of Tanzanian's candidacy for a", "start": 856.079, "duration": 5.041}, {"text": "non-permanent seat on the UN Security", "start": 858.56, "duration": 7.44}, {"text": "Council for the term 2029 2030 during", "start": 861.12, "duration": 8.0}, {"text": "elections to be held by this assembly in", "start": 866.0, "duration": 6.079}, {"text": "June 2028.", "start": 869.12, "duration": 6.399}, {"text": "I therefore seize this opportunity to", "start": 872.079, "duration": 6.961}, {"text": "formally announce our candidature.", "start": 875.519, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "During our tenure in the council, we", "start": 879.04, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "will put forward and prioritize", "start": 881.519, "duration": 6.161}, {"text": "deliberations on matters vital to the", "start": 884.16, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "maintainance of international peace and", "start": 887.68, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "security such as preventive diplomacy", "start": 889.76, "duration": 6.48}, {"text": "and the peaceful settlement of disputes.", "start": 892.88, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "Women in peacekeeping, youth in peace", "start": 896.24, "duration": 5.599}, {"text": "and security, and the reform of the", "start": 898.48, "duration": 6.799}, {"text": "United Nations peacekeeping.", "start": 901.839, "duration": 5.601}, {"text": "In the coming days,", "start": 905.279, "duration": 6.641}, {"text": "we will engage with each one of you and", "start": 907.44, "duration": 7.839}, {"text": "present our vision and respectfully seek", "start": 911.92, "duration": 6.4}, {"text": "your valued support to enable Tanzania", "start": 915.279, "duration": 6.961}, {"text": "to serve with a strong African voice,", "start": 918.32, "duration": 7.04}, {"text": "principled leadership, and unwavering", "start": 922.24, "duration": 6.159}, {"text": "commitment to international peace and", "start": 925.36, "duration": 6.039}, {"text": "security.", "start": 928.399, "duration": 3.0}, {"text": "Mr. President", "start": 931.519, "duration": 3.68}, {"text": "Tanzania is deeply concerned and", "start": 933.44, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "saddened by the protracted conflict and", "start": 935.199, "duration": 5.521}, {"text": "humanitarian suffering in Gaza and", "start": 938.56, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "across the Middle East. We continue to", "start": 940.72, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "call for the protection of civilians,", "start": 943.36, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "unhindered humanitarian assistance, and", "start": 945.68, "duration": 8.32}, {"text": "renewed diplomacy towards lasting peace.", "start": 948.24, "duration": 8.56}, {"text": "Tanzania remains firmly committed to the", "start": 954.0, "duration": 5.759}, {"text": "two-state solution with Israel and", "start": 956.8, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "Palestine living side by side in peace", "start": 959.759, "duration": 4.961}, {"text": "and harmony in accordance with", "start": 962.8, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "international law and relevant UN", "start": 964.72, "duration": 4.479}, {"text": "resolutions.", "start": 967.44, "duration": 4.399}, {"text": "We reaffir we reaffirm the right of the", "start": 969.199, "duration": 5.521}, {"text": "Palestinian people to self-determination", "start": 971.839, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "and believe that lasting peace must", "start": 974.72, "duration": 5.679}, {"text": "guarantee dignity, security, and", "start": 977.279, "duration": 7.92}, {"text": "legitimate aspiration of both peoples.", "start": 980.399, "duration": 7.041}, {"text": "We have been consistent on this for the", "start": 985.199, "duration": 6.88}, {"text": "past 50 years. For us, this is a matter", "start": 987.44, "duration": 7.839}, {"text": "of our foreign principle.", "start": 992.079, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "Mr. President,", "start": 995.279, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "on behalf of the people of the United", "start": 997.279, "duration": 5.521}, {"text": "Republic of Tanzania, I wish to pay", "start": 1000.079, "duration": 4.401}, {"text": "tribute to his excellency Antonio", "start": 1002.8, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "Gutirez as he concludes his", "start": 1004.48, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "distinguished tenure as Secretary", "start": 1007.04, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "General of the United Nations.", "start": 1009.12, "duration": 5.839}, {"text": "During his tenure, he steered the UN", "start": 1012.24, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "through an exceptionally challenging", "start": 1014.959, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "periods marked by conflicts,", "start": 1017.68, "duration": 6.079}, {"text": "geopolitical tensions, the coid9", "start": 1020.639, "duration": 6.32}, {"text": "pandemic, climate emergencies, and", "start": 1023.759, "duration": 7.521}, {"text": "growing pressure on multilateralism.", "start": 1026.959, "duration": 6.641}, {"text": "In all these situations,", "start": 1031.28, "duration": 7.559}, {"text": "he remained firm and undeterred.", "start": 1033.6, "duration": 5.239}, {"text": "Tanzania appreciates his support for", "start": 1048.16, "duration": 5.92}, {"text": "Africa's aspirations for peace,", "start": 1051.36, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "sustainable development, climate", "start": 1054.08, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "justice, and a fairer international", "start": 1056.48, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "financial architecture as well as his", "start": 1058.72, "duration": 6.56}, {"text": "personal engagement with our country.", "start": 1061.36, "duration": 6.559}, {"text": "Similar accolades are for Ambassador", "start": 1065.28, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "Amina Muhammad, Deputy Secretary", "start": 1067.919, "duration": 5.921}, {"text": "General, who has played a pivotal role", "start": 1070.32, "duration": 6.56}, {"text": "in advancing the SDGs, advocacy for", "start": 1073.84, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "women, children, and those whose voices", "start": 1076.88, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "are too often unheard.", "start": 1079.84, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "We shall miss your contribution,", "start": 1082.88, "duration": 6.24}, {"text": "but Africa is proud to welcome its own", "start": 1085.52, "duration": 6.72}, {"text": "daughter back home.", "start": 1089.12, "duration": 5.679}, {"text": "To both of you, we wish you every", "start": 1092.24, "duration": 6.08}, {"text": "success and fulfillment in the years", "start": 1094.799, "duration": 5.601}, {"text": "ahead.", "start": 1098.32, "duration": 5.599}, {"text": "Mr. President, in conclusion,", "start": 1100.4, "duration": 6.48}, {"text": "I wish to underscore that the UN must", "start": 1103.919, "duration": 5.681}, {"text": "not merely reflect on the balance of", "start": 1106.88, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "power, but serve as a platform for", "start": 1109.6, "duration": 7.439}, {"text": "justice, solidarity, and progress.", "start": 1112.24, "duration": 7.84}, {"text": "As we take stock of its invaluable", "start": 1117.039, "duration": 5.281}, {"text": "contribution to the advancement of", "start": 1120.08, "duration": 4.719}, {"text": "humanity, maintainance of international", "start": 1122.32, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "peace and security, social economic", "start": 1124.799, "duration": 5.201}, {"text": "progress and sustained development over", "start": 1127.28, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "the past 81 years. Let us be reminded", "start": 1130.0, "duration": 5.679}, {"text": "that there are more mountains to climb", "start": 1132.96, "duration": 6.079}, {"text": "and milestones to accomplish. Tanzania", "start": 1135.679, "duration": 6.481}, {"text": "believes that it is only by respecting", "start": 1139.039, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "and living by the charter that we can", "start": 1142.16, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "honor the past and build a safer and", "start": 1144.559, "duration": 6.24}, {"text": "better future for all. Thank you for", "start": 1147.84, "duration": 8.04}, {"text": "your attention. Asante Sana.", "start": 1150.799, "duration": 5.081}, {"text": "On behalf of the assembly, I wish to", "start": 1162.88, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "thank the vice president of the United", "start": 1165.36, "duration": 6.679}, {"text": "Republic of Tanzania.", "start": 1168.24, "duration": 3.799}]